"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff meeting on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility, leveraging AI for data visualization and real-time analytics. Key milestones include a call for R&D ideas by July 20th, team expansion with five new cybersecurity and cloud architecture specialists joining on September 10th, and a budget approval of $2M by the executive board, later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses. The project has progressed through design to development, led by Omar Jensen, and recently achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics. Security protocols were updated in January to include multi-factor authentication and encryption. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, with a detailed report scheduled for the staff meeting on November 20th."
